{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRootStructure","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoRootStructure","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoArgSector","lean:module:Mathlib.Topology.Order.IntermediateValue"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exists_pinning_data","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exists_pinning_data","kind":"theorem","line":444,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L444-L466","doc":"**Everything `branchInt_eq_zero_of_roots` assumed about the roots, supplied.**\n\nReturns the real root `t ∈ (0,1)`, the other two roots as complex numbers, the\nfactorisation certifying that these three *are* the roots — so a consumer\nholding only Vieta data can match against them — and the two sign facts. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_mul_otherRoots_fst_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_mul_otherRoots_fst_neg","kind":"theorem","line":394,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L394-L440","doc":"**The upper extra root too, once `c < 0`** — i.e. once `φ > π/2`.\n\nIn the real branch both roots are negative anyway, so `c < 0` is not used there.\nIn the conjugate branch it is exactly what turns `s·a < c·b` into\n`c·b + s·a < 2c·b < 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_mul_otherRoots_snd_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.im_mul_otherRoots_snd_neg","kind":"theorem","line":345,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L345-L392","doc":"**The lower extra root is pushed into the open lower half plane.**\n\nBoth branches land here: a negative real root gives `Im(x·y) = y·sin φ < 0`\ndirectly, and the conjugate pair gives it from `sa_lt_cb`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.otherRoots_factor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.otherRoots_factor","kind":"theorem","line":336,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L336-L341","doc":"The quadratic really does factor through these two. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.otherRoots_prod","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.otherRoots_prod","kind":"theorem","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L321-L334","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.otherRoots_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.otherRoots_sum","kind":"theorem","line":317,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L317-L319","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuous_otherRoots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.continuous_otherRoots","kind":"theorem","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L293-L315","doc":"**`otherRoots` is continuous — including THROUGH the collision.**\n\nBean `qou-glbl` part (b). The formula is piecewise on the sign of `β² − 4γ`, and\nthat is exactly where the two roots collide. It is nonetheless continuous, for\nthe reason that makes Gap A tractable at all: at `β² − 4γ = 0` **both branches\ngive `(−β/2, −β/2)`** — `Real.sqrt 0 = 0` on one side, and the imaginary part\nvanishes on the other.\n\nSo the *labelling* is continuous across the collision even though it is not\ndifferentiable there. That is the asymmetry `qou-glbl` turns on: continuity\nsurvives exactly what differentiability does not. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_deriv_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_deriv_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":283,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L283-L291","doc":"**The IFT's hypothesis holds at the real root**, in the form\n`exists_hasDerivAt_root` consumes: `3t² − 4ct + 2c+1 ≠ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_deriv_ge","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_deriv_ge","kind":"theorem","line":263,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L263-L281","doc":"**`∂p/∂y ≥ 7/4` at the real root** — so the IFT applies, and the `1.75`\nRoute 32 G8 measured is exactly `7/4`.\n\nTwo exact facts do it: the quartic satisfies\n`q(t) − 7/16 = (2t−1)²(9 + 4t − 4t²)/16 ≥ 0` on `(0,1)`, and `t(1−t) ≤ 1/4`.\nDividing, `∂p/∂y ≥ (7/16)/(1/4) = 7/4`. Equality would need `t = 1/2`, which is\nexcluded by `two_fifths_lt` only in the weak sense — the bound holds regardless. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_deriv_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_deriv_mul","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L255-L261","doc":"The `y`-derivative of `unitCubic`, times `t(1−t)`, is a **`c`-free quartic**.\nThe root relation eliminates `c` entirely. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.otherRoots","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.otherRoots","kind":"def","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L233-L242","doc":"The two roots of `Y² + βY + γ`, written down: a real pair when\n`β² ≥ 4γ`, a conjugate pair otherwise. Explicit rather than abstract, because\nthe whole point is to read off the sign of `Im(x·y)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.real_root_neg_of_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.real_root_neg_of_ne","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L209-L229","doc":"**Every real root of the cubic other than `t` is negative.** A corollary of\nthe above, recorded because it is the statement one wants to quote. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.W_nonneg_of_disc_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.W_nonneg_of_disc_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L188-L207","doc":"**If the other two roots are real, then `W ≥ 0`.**\n\nThe step with content. `hD` is the quadratic's discriminant, which is\nnonnegative exactly when it has a real root. Rearranged it says\n`W² ≥ 4t(1−t)²`; but `W < 0` caps `t` at the golden section while `c ≤ 1` floors\nit at `2/5`, and on `(2/5, (√5−1)/2)` the quartic `4t(1−t)² − W²` is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.two_fifths_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.two_fifths_lt","kind":"theorem","line":178,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L178-L186","doc":"**`c ≤ 1` forces the root above `2/5`.**\n\n`c ≤ 1` gives `t³ − 2t² + 3t − 1 ≥ 0` (multiplying by `t(t−1) < 0` flips), and\nthat cubic is strictly increasing with value `−7/125` at `2/5`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.gamma_rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.gamma_rel","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L174-L176","doc":"`t·γ = 1` for the quadratic factor's constant term `γ = t² − 2ct + 2c + 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.beta_rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.beta_rel","kind":"theorem","line":166,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L166-L172","doc":"**`β·t(1−t) = W`**, where `β = t − 2c` is the quadratic factor's linear\ncoefficient and `W = t² + t − 1`. Since `t(1−t) > 0` on `(0,1)`, `β` and `W`\nhave the same sign — which is how step 3 turns a statement about the\ndiscriminant into a statement about the roots. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.two_c_rel","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.two_c_rel","kind":"theorem","line":162,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L162-L164","doc":"`2c·t(t−1) = t³ + t − 1`, i.e. `p(t) = 0` solved for the `c`-terms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.re_le_one_of_normSq_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.re_le_one_of_normSq_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L156-L158","doc":"**`|x| = 1 → Re x ≤ 1`** — the hypothesis `c ≤ 1` above, supplied on the arc. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_root_lt_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_root_lt_one","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L145-L154","doc":"**No real root of `unitCubic c` reaches `1`**, for every `c ≤ 1`.\n\nThe measured max over the arc is `0.80193` (Route 36 G5), so the bound is true\nbut not tight. It does not need to be — `notCut` only asks for `< 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_pos_of_one_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_pos_of_one_le","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L134-L143","doc":"**`p(t) > 0` for every `t ≥ 1`, whenever `c ≤ 1`** — at least `1`, in fact. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_shift","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_shift","kind":"theorem","line":125,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L125-L132","doc":"**`p(1+s) = 1 + (4−2c)s + (3−2c)s² + s³`** — an identity in `c` and `s`.\n\nThe whole content of this subsection. Expanded about `t = 1` every coefficient is\npositive as soon as `c ≤ 1`, so positivity for `s ≥ 0` is immediate; expanded\nabout `t = 0` the signs are mixed and nothing is immediate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exists_root_mem_Ioo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.exists_root_mem_Ioo","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L102-L108","doc":"**There is a real root in `(0,1)`.** `p(0) = −1 < 0 < 1 = p(1)`, then IVT. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_one","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L98-L100","doc":"`p(1) = 1` **identically in `c`** — the `2c` terms cancel. This is why the\nroot in `(0,1)` costs nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic_zero","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L96-L96","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curve_eq_unitCubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.curve_eq_unitCubic","kind":"theorem","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L85-L94","doc":"**On `|x| = 1` the deformed curve's `y`-cubic IS `unitCubic (Re x)`.**\n\nChecked rather than asserted: the reduction rests on `2·Re x·x = x² + 1`, which\nis `x·conj x = 1` in disguise. Without this, everything below would be a correct\ntheorem about the wrong polynomial — the failure mode this lane has hit nine\ntimes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCircle_quadratic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCircle_quadratic","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L69-L83","doc":"**`2·(Re x)·x = x² + 1` on `|x| = 1`** — which is `x·conj x = 1` in disguise.\n\nExtracted as a theorem rather than left inside `curve_eq_unitCubic`, because it is\nalso the *minimal polynomial* of a non-real `x` on the circle over `ℝ`, and that\nis what reduces any polynomial in `x` to something linear with real\ncoefficients — used by `quintic_of_mul_real` in `FiveTwoTransport`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDeformedSaddle.unitCubic","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/FiveTwoRootStructure.lean#L66-L67","doc":"The `y`-cubic of the deformed curve on `|x| = 1`, monic, with `c = cos φ`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}